WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code builds a per-subject table of functional-connectivity
    similarity scores across several modeling conditions (different
    voxel/parcel scales, hyperparameter sources, and two additional model
    variants labeled SAR and rWW), pulling values from a simulation
    results CSV and a MATLAB file and averaging across a fixed set of task
    contrasts for each subject. It then runs a series of paired
    comparisons between specific pairs of these conditions, computing for
    each pair a paired t-test on the per-subject differences along with
    the sample size, mean difference, a 95 percent confidence interval,
    the t-statistic and degrees of freedom, the p-value, an effect size
    (Cohen's dz), and the count of subjects with a positive difference.
    Each row of the output table corresponds to one such pairwise contrast
    between two named conditions, summarizing how that pair's per-subject
    values differ across the group. Note that the code references two
